2025-06-05 14:59:20,397 - DEBUG - Processing raw tweet: {
  "uri": "https://x.com/webuildscore/status/1923425638490243295",
  "datetime": "2025-05-16T17:09:42+00:00",
  "source": "X",
  "label": null,
  "content": "Score is excited to welcome Kacper as our new Social Media Manager!\n\nKacper brings over four years of hands-on experience in Web3, crypto, e-commerce, and AI, working with early-stage startups, high-growth ventures, and established tech teams. Throughout his career, he\u2019s led the growth of social media accounts from 0 to 200k+ followers and managed communities of over 100k members, driving engagement and building loyal user bases across fast-moving, digital-native ecosystems.\n\nFrom growing his own Web3 projects to helping startups and established projects scale in the crypto and AI space, Kacper witnessed firsthand how attention, trust, and clarity make or break a project. This experience makes him a powerful addition to the Score team as we level up our social and community efforts and bridge the worlds of football, data, and decentralised tech.\n\nA word from Kacper:\n\"Web3 and AI are full of bold ideas - but not all of them solve real problems.\n\nAfter years of working in this space, you learn to see past the hype. Score Vision isn\u2019t another dashboard with fancy numbers. It\u2019s a decentralised computer vision framework that tackles one of football\u2019s biggest bottlenecks: access to high-quality analytics.\n\nFootball is a global game, but access to advanced analytics has been limited to the top clubs. Score fixes that. This isn\u2019t just a better tool - it\u2019s a paradigm shift. Score allows every club, scout, and analyst to see the game deeper, faster, and smarter.\n\nThat\u2019s the kind of change I want to be part of.\"",
  "user": {
