  "content": "We're excited to announce that @dsvfund has invested $100K OTC into @webuildscore, forming a strategic partnership between two entities aligned on $TAO's long-term vision and ethos.\n\nScore is building real-time video intelligence on Bittensor through Subnet 44, creating Vision-as-a-Service that transforms raw video into actionable insights. Starting with sports, where 90-minute football matches can be processed and labeled in under 3 seconds, the model scales across industries.\n\n\"We first met the Score team at TOKEN2049 in Dubai, and it quickly became clear they weren't just building another AI tool. They've got a sharp product, a tight vision, and a real plan to turn Subnet 44 into a commercial powerhouse,\" said DSV.\n\nAs Subnet 44 opens up to other verticals, it provides the infrastructure layer to become the optic nerve for AI, supporting the development of human-level AI and beyond.\n\n\"Siam and Mark bring exactly the kind of strategic thinking we need as we scale Score,\" said Nigel Grant  co-founder and Score's CSO. \"They understand the Bittensor ecosystem deeply and share our long-term vision for what decentralized AI can achieve. This partnership gives us the strategic support to navigate the complexities of building on $TAO while staying focused on our mission.\"\n\nThe partnership reflects DSV's visionary approach under @SiamKidd and @markcreaser's leadership, plus their understanding of navigating the $TAO & dTAO ecosystem, both the challenges and opportunities. \n\nThis represents a bridge between aligned entities committed to the long-term, positive-sum game that $TAO's core values represent.\n\nLooking ahead, Score is expanding beyond Subnet 44 as we train our Object Value Function model across other subnets and prepare to introduce new tasks to our miners pool. \n\nThis growth reflects our commitment to building infrastructure that serves the entire Bittensor ecosystem.\n\nYou can hear more about this vision when our CEO Maxime 