2025-06-12 12:36:17,469 - DEBUG - Processing raw tweet: {
  "uri": "https://x.com/webuildscore/status/1930611445852524855",
  "datetime": "2025-06-05T13:03:32+00:00",
  "source": "X",
  "label": null,
  "content": "We're excited to announce a game-changing addition to the Score leadership team: Matthew Karas is joining as our new Chief Innovation Officer!\n\nWith Matthew on the team, Score is adding a pioneer in real-time data, generative AI, and human-machine understanding. Over the past 36 years, he's taken ideas from algorithm design all the way through to globally scaled products.\n\nMatt served as CTO for ITV Player and was Head of Technology at BBC News Online, where he scaled to 1.5 billion monthly users over 28 years. He also created the world's first productised speech-based, frame-accurate AV search engine and sold it to HP. As a founder, Matt launched Dremedia, which was acquired by Autonomy and Co-founded FutureLearn, a MOOC platform used by 30+ top UK universities.\n\nAs an independent technologist, Matthew has guided over 40 companies, spanning media, healthcare, national security, and virtual environments, to turn complex ideas into scalable, searchable systems.\n\nA word from Matthew:\n\n\u201cI can't quite believe that the next phase of my career concerns football, as I have managed to get through the last 50 years without ever going to a match. However, the data problems are familiar. These are challenges I first tackled 20 years ago, extracting on-screen text from perimeter advertising and players' shirts.\n\nWhat applies to football applies wherever value comes from understanding fast-moving human beings: from festival crowds to transport hubs to urban warfare.\nSince first seeing what the Score team has already achieved and learning about the self-sustaining Bittensor marketplace for work, I feel this is the perfect environment for ongoing innovation.\u201d\n\nAt Score, we\u2019re building the Optic Nerve of AI. Our platform connects decentralized annotators to advanced computer-vision tasks, structuring data in real time. Powered by Bittensor, this network turns annotation into an open, incentive-based system where contributors and models grow together.\n\nMatthew\u2019s proven ability to turn pioneering technology into practical, global solutions makes him the ideal choice to drive Score\u2019s next phase. His arrival marks a major leap forward in our mission to redefine AI-powered computer vision intelligence.",
