  "source": "X",
  "label": null,
  "content": "Fractional kelly for sustained growth with less volatility:\n\nWhereas full kelly introduces risk for maximum growth, fractional kelly aims for growth in a risk-adjusted way, reducing the impact of a bad streak.\n\nFractional kelly could be implemented at any fraction of full kelly. E.g. 10%, 25%, 50%. The higher the percentage, the more risk you introduce.",
