  "datetime": "2025-07-18T13:04:37Z",
  "content": "Keypoints Scoring Update \u2013 Subnet 44\n\nWe\u2019ve rolled out a scoring update on the validation side of Subnet 44 to improve accuracy, stability, and resilience to noisy keypoint data from raw footage.\n\nWhat\u2019s new?\n\n\u2022 Smarter weighting of scoring components\n\u2022 Grading based on distance to pitch lines\n\u2022 Detection of whether players are actually on the field\n\nNew scoring weights:\n\n\u2022 On-line accuracy: 40%\n\u2022 Field placement: 20%\n\u2022 Keypoint quality: 25%\n\u2022 Stability & final output: 15%\n\nWe\u2019ve also introduced new scale factors that account for the spacing between keypoints relative to how spread out the players are, as well as the percentage of frames with valid homography projections.\n\nThese changes are part of our continuous refinement loop, making Subnet 44 more stable, more accurate, and better equipped to support decentralised annotation at scale.",
  "username": "webuildscore",
  "display_name": "Score",
  "user_id": "1816264150755979264",
