2025-08-04 20:22:45,697 - DEBUG - Processing raw tweet: {
  "uri": "https://x.com/webuildscore/status/1942516691767869634",
  "datetime": "2025-07-08T09:30:44+00:00",
  "source": "X",
  "label": null,
  "content": "Transforming Data into Insight: Introducing Ishdeep Chadha \u2014 Score\u2019s Data Engineer\n\nWe\u2019re delighted to formally introduce Ishdeep (@chadha_ishdeep), whose dual talent for large-scale data engineering and eye-catching football visuals bridges Score\u2019s internal data workflows with the stories we share across the football community.\n\nAfter earning a degree in Electrical, Electronics and Communications Engineering from Shiv Nadar University in 2022, Ishdeep joined UnitedHealth Group as a data engineer. Over 2\u00bd years, he built and optimised ETL pipelines in SQL, Python and multiple cloud services: a toolkit he later repurposed for football. Evenings found him breaking down Manchester City matches on X, publishing slick, insight-rich graphics that turned raw stats into stories fans could feel. He added deeper context on Medium, exploring metrics such as expected goals (xG) and other metrics that shape modern football.\n\nSome of that content landed in the feed of our CEO, Max. A quick DM turned into a trial project, and by March 2025, Ishdeep had joined Score full-time.\n\nToday, he supports both the data engineering and marketing teams by building robust pipelines, shaping internal dashboards, and providing input for visuals that power our social channels. Whether he\u2019s fine-tuning ingestion jobs or turning a possession map into a share-worthy graphic, his work connects deep data to everyday football conversations.\n\nA word from Ishdeep:\n\n\u201cI am passionate about leveraging data and technology to create innovative solutions that improve the quality and accessibility of services. I am motivated by the opportunity to work with a diverse and collaborative team of data engineers, analysts, and scientists at Score, where I can contribute to the company's vision. And sharing my love of football with the community and try to show my perspective on how we can use data to contribute to the sport's world.\u201d\n\nIshdeep\u2019s journey reflects what we value at Score: the power of independent initiative, technical precision, and a passion for the game. By pairing engineering rigour with football insight, Ishdeep is helping Score redraw what\u2019s possible in the game.",
