  "datetime": "2025-07-04T11:00:14+00:00",
  "source": "X",
  "label": null,
  "content": "From Miner to Builder: Introducing Mikha\u00ebl Brazier \u2014 Score\u2019s Subnet Engineer\n\nWe\u2019re excited to formally introduce Mikha\u00ebl, our dedicated Subnet Engineer. Since joining Score in February, he has overseen every aspect of our subnet, from upkeep to performance optimisation.\n\nBut Mikha\u00ebl\u2019s Bittensor journey began long before his official start date. For more than a year prior to joining Score, he mined on multiple Bittensor subnets, including the subnet preceding Score Vision. That hands-on work with decentralised compute gave him deep expertise and a front-row seat to the power of open machine-learning networks.\n\nBuilding on his strong foundation in data science and AI for business, Mikha\u00ebl leapt from contributor to builder at a pivotal moment in Score\u2019s evolution.\n\nA word from Mikha\u00ebl:\n\n\u201cI joined Score Vision because I saw more than a subnet, I saw a challenge worth obsessing over. Turning raw video into structured intelligence, and doing it all in a decentralised system with the goal to reward efficiency and precision. It felt like the right place to push my limits.\u201d\n\nMikha\u00ebl\u2019s journey reflects the spirit of the network itself. Start at the edge, build from the inside. His technical depth and alignment with our mission make him a key force as we evolve the subnet, expand our capabilities, and continue building the Optic Nerve of AI.",
